      {
        "title": "Some critical issues with the SWE-bench dataset | Hacker News",
        "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=43130732",
        "description": "| |  | | --- | | Some critical issues with the SWE-bench dataset (arxiv.org) | | 350 points by joshwa on Feb 21, 2025 | hide | past | favorite | 116 comments |     |  |  | | --- | --- | | |  | | --- | | comex on Feb 21, 2025  | next )   Some of the examples in the paper seem to be wrong. For django-31056, they claim the AI-generated patch is \"incomplete\" because it's \"missing critical parts of this logic, such as the try-except block and the check for a running event loop.\". The human patch is more idiomatic, but it's also more confusing, as shown by the fact that it confused the authors of this paper.",
